Package: next-installer
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: m68k
Installer-Menu-Item: 7400
Maintainer: next68k-linux <https://github.com/dannydorazio/next68k-linux>
Depends: cdebconf-udeb, di-utils, installed-base, next-partitioner
Provides: bootable-system
Section: debian-installer
Priority: standard
Description: Install the NeXT kernel and make the disk bootable
 Installs the NeXT Linux kernel package into the new system, which writes
 the kernel into the disk's boot partition (its zz-next-boot hook), along
 with the NeXT's settings for Debian (from next68k-linux's debian-root/).
 The disk's boot blocks, the loader the ROM starts, were written by
 next-partitioner.  Takes the place of a boot loader installer.
